{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project","id":1197883,"title":"Advice on a Hermetic Project","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-20T21:20:39-07:00","id":1197883,"title":"Advice on a Hermetic Project","content":"Recently, i started a thread for developing a setting for a CWoD story. This setting was a summer camp called Camp David, which is in the Everglades. One suggestion i got was to make the founder of the camp a Hermetic who did it to subtly teach Hermetic Doctrine to younger generations. I thought the idea was pretty decent and i decided to make this Hermetic Gentleman the founder of the Junior Foresters, the Boy Scout-like organization that owns and runs the camp. I already have a basic idea for the Junior Forester's history and the way the Hermetic's run it. But, i need help figuring out how the Hermetics could subtly teach Hermetic Doctrine in a Boy Scout's-like organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T23:53:25-07:00","id":1197898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project#post1197883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recently, i started a thread for developing a setting for a CWoD story. This setting was a summer camp called Camp David, which is in the Everglades. One suggestion i got was to make the founder of the camp a Hermetic who did it to subtly teach Hermetic Doctrine to younger generations. I thought the idea was pretty decent and i decided to make this Hermetic Gentleman the founder of the Junior Foresters, the Boy Scout-like organization that owns and runs the camp. I already have a basic idea for the Junior Forester's history and the way the Hermetic's run it. But, i need help figuring out how the Hermetics could subtly teach Hermetic Doctrine in a Boy Scout's-like organization.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What House is he?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T06:29:06-07:00","id":1197956,"title":"","content":"If you haven't decided it yet, the general idea of boy scout cap gives me a Tytalus or Flambeau vive. Any House likes to teach but the nature setting gives me more of a survivalist vive, learn from experiece, teach discipline, that sort of stuff.<br /> <br /> Teaching Hermetic doctrine, in general, could involve herbology (occult properties of plants) astronomy (astrology) and the legends of the supernatural that happens in the woods to give that extra wonder.<br /> <br /> Personally I find the idea of senior members in dark robes going to chant in a clearing when the stars are right to be quite alluring, and would bend reality to make that happen.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-21-2018, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T08:42:11-07:00","id":1197984,"title":"","content":"Flamebeau could be a interesting patron, so could Tytalus. But, what would keep House Tytalus from treating the Foresters the same way they treat their apprentices? Because, you can only go so far until a parent complains.<br /> <br /> Also, the image of Senior Foresters doing rituals is pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T08:49:17-07:00","id":1197987,"title":"","content":"Maybe start to incorporate some of the more &quot;mainstream&quot; Hermetic practices into the curriculum? Giving out Astrology and Mythology Merit Badges to slowly help kids understand the Hermetic way of thinking. Those that show aptitude are approached for apprenticeship. Those that aren't might still covertly be taught minor sorcery without anyone realizing it. And slowly, their personal Paradigms begin to shift.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Senpai liked my idea! Hooray! </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T09:09:08-07:00","id":1197996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1197984#post1197984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flamebeau could be a interesting patron, so could Tytalus. But, what would keep House Tytalus from treating the Foresters the same way they treat their apprentices? Because, you can only go so far until a parent complains.<br /> <br /> Also, the image of Senior Foresters doing rituals is pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Parents can't complain if you use mind magick on them. This is why I asked what house a Tytalus based setup would be on par with many of those &quot;teen recovery&quot; or &quot;conversion&quot; camps which are just a steady string of abuse and horror of course the tytalus mage is trying hone the child's rebelious spirit to have them rise up rather than out of mere cruelty and averice.<br /> <br /> Flambeau are wizard-knights and might readily incorporate chivalric bits. Outside any hermetic bits they will also definately teach you to fight.<br /> <br /> Bonsagius well the question here would be ultimately is this about teaching and the future of the order.. or is this an experiment?<br /> <br /> Quaesitori would incorporate a combination of investigation tactics and a sense of justice, teaching debate and fact checking.<br /> <br /> Of the smaller houses under ex misc I'd suggest two readily available options:<br /> <br /> House Mercere, in ars magica this was the house to groom mundanes as aids to the Order so incorporating its red hats and broad method of teaching might be interesting.<br /> <br /> House Mertina, this gives you crossover fun! They are the House that studies the Fae if you want to bring in changeling effects this would be a good one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T10:22:03-07:00","id":1198025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, what would keep House Tytalus from treating the Foresters the same way they treat their apprentices? Because, you can only go so far until a parent complains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tytalus House has a well earned reputation, but I can believe that one can resist the temptation of being <i>stupidly </i>rough and breaking all the children.<br /> <br /> A Tytalus <b>covert </b>training has to test the waters, going exactly far enough so the parents won't complain, and then going far beyond that <i>when/if </i>the foresters are ready. That is, when/if they're willing to go to any lenghts to learn the secret truths. At that pioint the boy it's part of a secret occult conspiracy, and isn't about to complain to their parents any more than a regular Acolyte.<br /> <br /> Of those boys that don't seem strong enough, well, they will get as much of a rough treatment as it's reasonable in a 20th century boy scout camp so they return relatively &quot;better&quot; as defined by a Tytalan. (I don't know how far you can go. Mind magick it's there if things go really bad, but I imagine the Mage would preffer to not brainwash everyone, on the grounds that it can fail).<br /> <br /> As an idea, you could use the reward system. If some badges are <i>really </i>hard to get, well, it's not like you have to catch 'em all. But it's tempting. More and more esoterical badges could test the willpower, smarts, and willingness to believe in the supernatural. The hardest of them all could involve a covert initiation that would test if &quot;the boy is ready&quot; (best said in a spectral voice under a black hood). Only *then* would Mind magick be used to see if the loyalty it's genuine, and erase the memories if it's not (minimizing it's need only to those few that pass the initiation and want to join).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-21-2018, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:21:33-07:00","id":1198087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198025#post1198025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tytalus House has a well earned reputation, but I can believe that one can resist the temptation of being <i>stupidly </i>rough and breaking all the children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tytalus abuse is about on par with any other &quot;Teen bootcamp&quot; in the real world. Those places are fucked up. Honestly the Mage at least isn't doing it out of jackassery and greed so its probably not as bad as those places which.. in the world of Darkness probably are subsidaries of Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:28:57-07:00","id":1198093,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggedtion Alph. No matter what house controls the Junior Foresters, the Foresters as a organization will still be affected by Hermetic politics. Especially because Sir Reginald Fields, the founder of The Foresters and a known member of House Flambeau, House Tytalus or House Quaesitori stated in his will that any Hermetic of a certain rank of any house could become Grand Master of The Foresters after the previous one dies or retires. Surprisingly, this had led to a lot of heated arguements over the years after the death or retirement of the Grand Masters and who will replace them. I actually have a plothook based on this kind of situation, want to hear it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 03-21-2018, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:30:58-07:00","id":1198095,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but one thing it's your Apprentice, whom you entrust the powers of the universe and which actions reflect upon your rep. (and had better be elite) and another thing it's to torture other people's kids.<br /> I would think that the mage would be worse to the first and far more lenient to the latter (albeit probably the kids would think of him as pretty harsh anyway because they just don't know how far the abuse can go).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:29:51-07:00","id":1198121,"title":"","content":"Your hermetic teachers and staff could teach Incantations to their campers, most likely all aimed at survival in the wilderness or even placating a spirit or two who might feel crossed by some kind of a action they did.<br /> <br /> The location could be a powerful natural node, or not far from one in the woods. That might be where the seniors do their rites, also teaching kids herbology and doing scavenger hunts where the campers are hunting warded Tass. If the campers are even a little spiritually aware they might pick out the Tass infused object in the tall grass or hidden from prying eyes. Those campers who found the Tass or even found different Tass might get a crash course in hedge magic in the form of Enchantment, turning that piece of precious stone into a bracelet with a little magic to it and get a special Merit Badge for this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T15:28:56-07:00","id":1198146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198095#post1198095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but one thing it's your Apprentice, whom you entrust the powers of the universe and which actions reflect upon your rep. (and had better be elite) and another thing it's to torture other people's kids.<br /> I would think that the mage would be worse to the first and far more lenient to the latter (albeit probably the kids would think of him as pretty harsh anyway because they just don't know how far the abuse can go).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apprenticeship starts before awakening. But more I was pointing to Teen bootcamps have pretty much proven to be completely horrible IRL, a Tytalus could get away with pretty high levels of abuse up to and including accidental death and not be as bad as them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:30:01-07:00","id":1198175,"title":"","content":"Regarding the creator's House, Bonisagus might work, given their focus on research and expanding into new frontiers. Alternately, House Merinita, who in addition to their focus on the fey also study nature magic, or possibly House Jerbiton for their focus on mundane society, arts and classical studies. <br /> <br /> As far as teaching goes, probably starting with the basic ethics and morals of the Order and the striving for personal excellence and discipline. Probably camping and wilderness survival skills, wood and nature lore, natural history, hand crafts and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T21:06:13-07:00","id":1198238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198175#post1198175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the creator's House, Bonisagus might work, given their focus on research and expanding into new frontiers. Alternately, House Merinita, who in addition to their focus on the fey also study nature magic, or possibly House Jerbiton for their focus on mundane society, arts and classical studies.<br /> <br /> As far as teaching goes, probably starting with the basic ethics and morals of the Order and the striving for personal excellence and discipline. Probably camping and wilderness survival skills, wood and nature lore, natural history, hand crafts and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, someone actually suggested House Jerbiton as the founder's house. Both that and House Merinita could work excellently. I have narrowed down the potential houses to House Flamebeau, Quaesitori, Bonisagus or Merinita. Also, how do you think the rest of the Traditions would react to the Junior Forester's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T21:09:44-07:00","id":1198239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198238#post1198238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, someone actually suggested House Jerbiton as the founder's house. Both that and House Merinita could work excellently. I have narrowed down the potential houses to House Flamebeau, Quaesitori, Bonisagus or Merinita. Also, how do you think the rest of the Traditions would react to the Junior Forester's?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that most of the Traditions would see the organization as a spectacular way to introduce new generations to their way of thinking. The issue, as always, comes from <i>who </i>gets to help the Hermetics foster this new generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T21:31:28-07:00","id":1198242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198239#post1198239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that most of the Traditions would see the organization as a spectacular way to introduce new generations to their way of thinking. The issue, as always, comes from <i>who </i>gets to help the Hermetics foster this new generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of the Traditions i can see actually wanting to cooperate with the Hermetics the top amongst them will probably be the Verbena and possibly The Dreamspeakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T21:42:37-07:00","id":1198243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198242#post1198242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of the Traditions i can see actually wanting to cooperate with the Hermetics the top amongst them will probably be the Verbena and possibly The Dreamspeakers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depending on how the focus works out I can suggest other Traditions: Akashics are almost a no brainer I mean Martial arts Camp is already a thing. Same with the Chorus and Jesus Camp. The less obvious one I am going to offer up, the Society of Ether. Now you might scoff at this as the stereotype of the tradition is lab bound madmen, but there's a whole sub faction built around the Gentleman adventurer who goes out into the unknown who scientifically study other factions and are readily assumed to be able to science their way with a swiss army knife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T21:56:55-07:00","id":1198247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198243#post1198243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depending on how the focus works out I can suggest other Traditions: Akashics are almost a no brainer I mean Martial arts Camp is already a thing. Same with the Chorus and Jesus Camp. The less obvious one I am going to offer up, the Society of Ether. Now you might scoff at this as the stereotype of the tradition is lab bound madmen, but there's a whole sub faction built around the Gentleman adventurer who goes out into the unknown who scientifically study other factions and are readily assumed to be able to science their way with a swiss army knife.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, The Chrous was actually high on my list of the Traditions possibly cooperating with the Junior Forestet's,project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T06:27:17-07:00","id":1198308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198243#post1198243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Gentleman adventurer who goes out into the unknown who scientifically study other factions and are readily assumed to be able to science their way with a swiss army knife.</div> </div> </div> </div>A cheerful gentleman that teaches everything about the natural world, can fight with bears barehanded, and tells campfire stories about paranormal activities.<br /> Best teacher ever. Also he could build games for the kids.<br /> <br /> This could work great as a multi-tradition thing.<br /> <br /> But having such awesome personel, I would want to play with them instead of the kids <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (well, I'm biased because I love the adventurers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T07:21:33-07:00","id":1198318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198243#post1198243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depending on how the focus works out I can suggest other Traditions: Akashics are almost a no brainer I mean Martial arts Camp is already a thing. Same with the Chorus and Jesus Camp. The less obvious one I am going to offer up, the Society of Ether. Now you might scoff at this as the stereotype of the tradition is lab bound madmen, but there's a whole sub faction built around the Gentleman adventurer who goes out into the unknown who scientifically study other factions and are readily assumed to be able to science their way with a swiss army knife.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got this image in my head of a pair of teachers (and good friends), one a Dreamspeaker and one an Etherite that teach kids self sufficiency, respect for nature and culture, and ingenuity. But it is the Dreamspeaker who has the whatever-works, seat-of-the-pants pragmatism (&quot;If it works and you didn't piss anyone off, you succeeded&quot;) and the Etherite who teaches the meticulous respect for tools and tradition (&quot;You heard but you don't really understand it until it's bitten you a few times, so take the time to be careful now so you have a nose later'). That combo would be really good at teaching kids respect for stories and tradition and also subtly promote their respect for the mysterious.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T13:22:41-07:00","id":1198391,"title":"","content":"Whether just a Hermetic thing or a cross-Tradition thing, I don't think the camps would teach the Foresters any kind of hedge magic until they reach the oldest age bracket (ages 18+; the equivalent to the Rover Scouts and Ranger Guides). This is because every formalized magical group understands from experience how dangerous magical knowledge can be, and why, therefore, a potential initiate into the mysteries must reach a certain level of emotional maturity. And while the camp itself can work wonders towards grooming kids into the ideal starting place, there are certain aspects of being a mature adult that only come with time and experience. This is why most secret societies chose to restrict membership to adults, and why the Lions of Zion (as with their Real Life Kabbalistic counterparts) require the initiate to be even older (into their 40s for when they can learn the real secrets).<br /> <br /> So regardless of who runs the Junior Foresters, they aren't going to sanction instruction in substantive magical knowledge until the Foresters have become adults. Exceptions to this would be limited to rituals of Countermagic, and the Warding parts of the Path of Summoning, Binding, and Warding.<br /> <br /> Rather, the Foresters are going to be learning both mundane practical Talents/Skills/Knowledges, as well as ideas about magical worldviews and things like Occult and Esoterica. Maybe even certain Lore specialities - for potential run-ins with Werewolves and Wraiths and Fey - and Cosmology (even Etiquette), for when dealing with the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Even then, the truly esoteric stuff would need to be restricted. After all, this is a program where normal children from normal families will show up. And kids talk, sometimes too much. Too much secrecy pertaining to the whole program would raise suspicion from parents and authorities. So if it's going to work, there needs to be multiple layers of initiation. The bulk of the Foresters learn practical skills and are introduced to the worldview. Merit badges and activities related to the occult and esoteric, however, are kept as a secret, secondary layer of initiation. Of course, kids being kids, everyone will know about the &quot;secret merit badges&quot;. Which is why this second layer acts as a smokescreen for yet a third layer, where the meat of the work is done. That way, whenever anyone talks about the &quot;secret badges&quot;, the uninitiated will presume they are always talking about layer 2, not even imagining that there's a third, even more secretive set of information that only very dedicated and committed Foresters are privy to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:59:32-07:00","id":1198413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198391#post1198391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether just a Hermetic thing or a cross-Tradition thing, I don't think the camps would teach the Foresters any kind of hedge magic until they reach the oldest age bracket (ages 18+; the equivalent to the Rover Scouts and Ranger Guides). This is because every formalized magical group understands from experience how dangerous magical knowledge can be, and why, therefore, a potential initiate into the mysteries must reach a certain level of emotional maturity. And while the camp itself can work wonders towards grooming kids into the ideal starting place, there are certain aspects of being a mature adult that only come with time and experience..</div> </div> </div> </div>For the majority of existence the Order of Hermes took in children and raised them &quot;In the order&quot; now that has become less of a thing since the Rise of the Order of Reason but it is a founding concept of the the Tradition. I'd also argue that an Etherite maybe abit fuzzy on the edges of &quot;Sleeper only&quot; science. I mean when you teach someone to turn a microwave into a Deathray.. its hard to say where the line is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:57:09-07:00","id":1198502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198413#post1198413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the majority of existence the Order of Hermes took in children and raised them &quot;In the order&quot; now that has become less of a thing since the Rise of the Order of Reason but it is a founding concept of the the Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Raising them in the order&quot; =/= &quot;immediately teaching them High Sorcery&quot;.<br /> <br /> People take in orphans and stray children all the time. That doesn't mean they usher them inside and promptly hand them a loaded gun. Even if they happen to be a family that believes in guns. They spend time training the children with firearms first, and only AFTER the kid is old enough to understand the gravity of the death machine they are using.<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes believes that magic is dangerous when in the hands of someone who doesn't know what they're doing. The reason for the Order's disdain for many of their fellow Traditions and especially capital-o Orphans is because many of those other mages display no discipline, control, or methodology. To the Hermetics, it's like drunk kids driving around at high speeds, at night, with expired learner's permits and the Wizard tied down in the back seat. This is why the Hermetic learning process is as protracted and difficult as it is. If a person has to struggle through volumes of theory, learn several languages, and spend hours performing mind-numbing rites and calculations, so be it. It just means that only the dedicated, disciplined, intelligent, and motivated will learn magic, and all others will wash out of the program.<br /> <br /> THAT is why I say that the Junior Foresters wouldn't be taught anything more than theory. There's a difference between establishing a foundation of knowledge, and handing over the secrets to reordering the universe. This is as true in the modern day as it was a thousand years ago. You don't hand a ten year old a gun, and you don't teach that ten year old how to summon umbrood or throw fireballs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd also argue that an Etherite maybe abit fuzzy on the edges of &quot;Sleeper only&quot; science. I mean when you teach someone to turn a microwave into a Deathray.. its hard to say where the line is. </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. The line is &quot;teaching a child how to make a death ray&quot;. See the above about not handing a child a gun.<br /> <br /> The progressive scientists of the Society of Ether are not the mad scientists from Genius: The Transgression. Etherites have unconventional understanding of science, but they aren't insane. At least, not categorically so. The Dissident faction notwithstanding, the Tradition is made of people who have a modicum of sense. That means knowing that while promoting a belief in capital-s Science(!) is important, there's a time and place to start learning children how to wield that kind of power. The Society of Ether has an ethics board for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-22-2018, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:06:35-07:00","id":1198522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198502#post1198502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Raising them in the order&quot; =/= &quot;immediately teaching them High Sorcery&quot;.<br /> <br /> People take in orphans and stray children all the time. That doesn't mean they usher them inside and promptly hand them a loaded gun. Even if they happen to be a family that believes in guns. They spend time training the children with firearms first, and only AFTER the kid is old enough to understand the gravity of the death machine they are using.<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes believes that magic is dangerous when in the hands of someone who doesn't know what they're doing. The reason for the Order's disdain for many of their fellow Traditions and especially capital-o Orphans is because many of those other mages display no discipline, control, or methodology. To the Hermetics, it's like drunk kids driving around at high speeds, at night, with expired learner's permits and the Wizard tied down in the back seat. This is why the Hermetic learning process is as protracted and difficult as it is. If a person has to struggle through volumes of theory, learn several languages, and spend hours performing mind-numbing rites and calculations, so be it. It just means that only the dedicated, disciplined, intelligent, and motivated will learn magic, and all others will wash out of the program.<br /> <br /> THAT is why I say that the Junior Foresters wouldn't be taught anything more than theory. There's a difference between establishing a foundation of knowledge, and handing over the secrets to reordering the universe. This is as true in the modern day as it was a thousand years ago. You don't hand a ten year old a gun, and you don't teach that ten year old how to summon umbrood or throw fireballs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to assume the only options are &quot;they start teaching real magic at 18+ or 10 yearolds with fireballs!&quot; Its quite possible to teach someone over 8 years magic rather than you know start completely when they are 18&quot;. There are plenty of people who teach their children to respectfully learn to use weapons when they are young, people's first hunts at 12 or so.<br /> <br /> So yeah I'd consider a slow burn from nothing to Third degree intiate potentially(that's starting mage btw) as dooable specifically because their regemine was built to do that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No it isn't. The line is &quot;teaching a child how to make a death ray&quot;. See the above about not handing a child a gun.<br /> <br /> The progressive scientists of the Society of Ether are not the mad scientists from Genius: The Transgression. Etherites have unconventional understanding of science, but they aren't insane. At least, not categorically so. The Dissident faction notwithstanding, the Tradition is made of people who have a modicum of sense. That means knowing that while promoting a belief in capital-s Science(!) is important, there's a time and place to start learning children how to wield that kind of power. The Society of Ether has an ethics board for a reason. </div> </div> </div><br /> And there's teaching them sleeper science. at 14 I know I did Fun chemistry experiments when supervised that were quite potentially dangerous if we weren't so supervised. Teaching Chemistry alone will give potential, lets also talk about teaching electronics or welding. Etherites don't see a solid line there so a kid who picks up some linear science while being taught chemistry or electronics or physics.. is something they probably won't notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:19:00-07:00","id":1198551,"title":"","content":"I do agree with Blu on not teaching the children and teen Foresters Hedge Magic immediatley. Since learning about magic could possibly break their brains combined with the threat of the Technocracy showing up and trashing everthing if they find out about Foresters using magic.<br /> <br /> I am wondering what a Celestial Chorister could teach without revealing his magic to Foresters besides the love of the One?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T00:37:20-07:00","id":1198575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198551#post1198551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree with Blu on not teaching the children and teen Foresters Hedge Magic immediatley. Since learning about magic could possibly break their brains combined with the threat of the Technocracy showing up and trashing everthing if they find out about Foresters using magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy doesn't magically show up and beat up every hedge mage out there. I mean there's a BIG difference between &quot;you have 1 dot of enchantment and 2 or 3 rituals&quot; say if you started a system to push one dot at 14 and one dot every year til 19 you'd have starting level Sorcerers. This also where they might jump to awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am wondering what a Celestial Chorister could teach without revealing his magic to Foresters besides the love of the One? </div> </div> </div>Anything, you can find a religious tradition irl that finds god/sacredness in just about anything. Moral philosophy, debate, survival, developing a sense of loyalty to your fellow man rather than &quot;I got mine&quot; attitudes, fencing, horse back riding, Vampire Recognition(an always useful skill in the world of darkness!), Singing, cooking, Gardening, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:35:06-07:00","id":1198646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy doesn't magically show up and beat up every hedge mage out there. I mean there's a BIG difference between &quot;you have 1 dot of enchantment and 2 or 3 rituals&quot; say if you started a system to push one dot at 14 and one dot every year til 19 you'd have starting level Sorcerers. This also where they might jump to awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the age limit would be, OoH would only teach magic to the most dedicated, willful and mentally capable. And these are capable of keeping a secret.<br /> <br /> I would argue that instead of placing a strict age limit they would test their capabilities. As a sort of mental &quot;you have to be this tall to enter&quot;, the test would keep most children out merely because it's too hard for children.<br /> Very excceptional teenagers may be rewarded with magic, but most of the lot would be 18+ merely because most children won't have the metal strenght and dedication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:17:54-07:00","id":1198734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198575#post1198575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy doesn't magically show up and beat up every hedge mage out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because the Technocracy doesn't KNOW about every hedge wizard. Their secrecy and subtlety is key to their survival, and both Sorcerer books have explicitly stated this as being the case. Any effort to train people in Sorcery, therefore, must be done with the utmost secrecy, or they risk attracting the Union's attention. Especially if it's a Traditions effort, because the Union keeps an eye out for their sorts of magical methods. Every camp that advertises itself as being religious or devoted to martial arts, for instance, gets flagged by automated systems as being worth keeping an eye on.<br /> <br /> Hell, the fact that this is a Sorcery-training program that exists as a Public organization makes secrecy all the more important. At least with secret societies or one-on-one apprenticeships, there's a limited visibility inherent in the arrangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T18:29:48-07:00","id":1198921,"title":"","content":"I can totally see the people in charge of The Junior Foresters doing everything in their power to hide the organization's true purpose from the Technocrats. Especially since that if they actually get their shit together for once, the Technos could easily shut down the Organization.<br /> <br /> Also, this may be weird to say, but evem though the Verbena would want to get involved to teach children about respecting nature, i am kinda seeing some of the other Traditions, mostly the OoH not really trusting them around the Foresters. I should determine why though.<br /> <br /> Also, i am planning a Mage plothook which involves the head of the Junior Foresters passing away and, in the election within the Organization to replace him, a mage from House Ngoma or House Hong Lei announces his candidacy. This raises eyebrows withing the Organization, especially with the OoH mages, due to the fact that those houses never showed much interest in the Junior Rangers project until now. So, the mage PCs are charged with figuring out why this canidate is running and what motivation would his house have for letting him run in the first place.<br /> <br /> Can i have advice on the motivations of House Ngoma or House Hong Lei?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T19:22:30-07:00","id":1198932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198921#post1198921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i have advice on the motivations of House Ngoma or House Hong Lei?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, House Ngoma was originally conceived with the idea that, a) the Ngoma have always been around (mostly in Southern and Eastern Africa), even after leaving the Grand Convocation; b) were exploring new ways to take advantage of their home cultures' migrations into Europe, the Americas and other places; c) had a somewhat grandiose plan of getting their foot into the door of the Traditions so they could eventually become the 10th Tradition (and possibly save the universe or something), and d) were willing to help House Shaea flex their new found political muscle to accomplish this (while also enjoying the idea of showing up some of the Hermetic old guard with their own ritual magic traditions). They were really always meant to be Hermetics-in-name-only, even if their exposure to certain aspects of European Hermeticism during the zenith of the British Empire means they understand what the Order is on about and may have adapted some of their methods (looking for potential new recruits in African-American colleges and fraternities/sororities, for example). <br /> <br /> Hong Lei were really intended to be a small group of syncretic weirdoes born out of the unique cultures of upper class 20th century Hong Kong and its mix of British and Chinese cultures. Upper class people of Chinese ethnicity who attended Eton, Oxford and the like before coming back to Hong Kong to work in major family businesses and join super exclusive social clubs, and during this process got recruited into the Order, usually in various Houses (Tytalus, Bonisagus, etc.) until a cabal of them decided they wanted to form their own House inside ExMisc mixing their Hermetic Arts with various traditional Chinese practices. Part of this includes mixing the traditional Hermetic ideas of Ascension with Taoist ideas of divine immortality. 20 years ago, there were only about a dozen or so of them; now they may be at about twice that. <br /> <br /> Someone from Ngoma might feel that the Junior Rangers should take a larger focus on bringing inner city youth out into the wilderness, and may look favorably on any group with a respect for traditions and the passing on of classical wisdom (even more so if this includes a healthy respect for ones ancestors). <br /> <br /> Someone from Hong Lei could be doing it because divination had revealed that this offers a potential path to power and influence in harmony with the will of heaven with the added bonus that he will look totally awesome while doing it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T19:12:09-07:00","id":1199563,"title":"","content":"You know, out of all the Trads, the only one I can't see getting involved is the Euthanatos. Because, assassins who practice death magic and Boy Scouts do not mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T19:36:09-07:00","id":1199565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1199563#post1199563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, out of all the Trads, the only one I can't see getting involved is the Euthanatos. Because, assassins who practice death magic and Boy Scouts do not mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey now, let's not be too hasty.<br /> <br /> First, not all Euthanatoi are assassins. Death is only one part of a larger Wheel, and many Euthanatoi would never engage themselves in dispensing the Good Death, even if they understand the need for it.<br /> <br /> Second, even assassins have useful things they could teach kids. After all, the types of skills involved in investigating people, stalking them, and preparing for the kill, also have some overlap with wilderness survival.<br /> <br /> Third, while the Euthanatos is preoccupied with death, they are arguably the most moral Tradition. They understand more than most how heavy the cost of killing is, and so hold themselves to the highest standards. If anyone were to attempt to teach children responsibility and personal discipline, it's these guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T21:06:26-07:00","id":1199575,"title":"","content":"And one of the sub-organizations of the Boy Scouts in the United States, the Order of the Arrow, is about cheerful service to others. I'm not going to divulge details from my time in the Scouts and as a Brotherhood Member of the Order of the Arrow, but the point of the Ordeal is to prepare oneself for service.<br /> <br /> All of the Traditions could get behind the general idea of the Order of the Arrow. The Order of Hermes would definitely find it a good place for recruits.<br /> <br /> As for how well this Hermetic Project works, remember that Scout troops differ in their effectiveness at teaching morals and thinking and teamwork. Some troops have good leaders who develop boys into good young men and other troops are badly lead.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Boy Scouts had a Fingerprinting merit badge at one point and do offer badges in a variety of fields, so a Euthanatoi could learn a lot in the Scouts.<br /> <br /> As an Outer Mystery, this isn't a bad one. The Hermetics will have to figure out who's blindly Obedient and who is Obedient and curious so they can decide which candidates to move into the inner circles and on the fast-track to Ascension.<br /> <br /> Order of the Arrow secrecy link:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://oa-scouting.org/themes/oascouting-theme/images/og/oa-social-stamp-og.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents\" target=\"_blank\"> Ask the Chairman - Ordeal Guests/Parents </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents\" target=\"_blank\"> https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Q: Hello Mike, I was wondering if there is any specific policy regarding having non-member guests and parents attend an Ordeal banquet. In the past, we have been allowing guests to come to our Ordeal banquet, which is held right after the Ordeal ceremony on Saturday night. This is when we also do our new member orientation. We figured that it would be best if parents could attend the orientation so they could get information about the Order of the Arrow. However, we have been receiving guests who are not parents and who are non-members. This has presented some problems as sometimes we have difficulty preventing some non-members from attending the Ordeal ceremony, and we had to tailor our orientation so it does not reveal any safeguarded material. Is there any policy or recommendation regarding whether guests are allowed at the Ordeal banquet after the Ordeal ceremony, and whether they are allowed to attend the new member orientation? Thank you for your help. In WWW, Elliott A: Elliott, The simple answer is that there is no prohibitive policy on such guests. Many lodges encourage the attendance of parents and Scout leaders at the banquet/orientation. I think it is a great strategy to get parents and other responsible parties really engaged and understanding the importance of membership in the Order. What the National OA Committee has been clear about is who should attend the actual ceremony. My suggestion is that you police that attendance carefully. I pulled out a couple statements from the 2015 printing of the Order of the Arrow Handbook that you might reference. Page 34 of the 2015 edition states: &ldquo;Youth and adult candidates for membership into the Order of the Arrow are introduced to the Order&rsquo;s concepts of servant leadership through a safeguarded ceremonial induction. Non-members should not attend the ceremonies. The Order of the Arrow recognizes and respects the right of any parent, Scout leader, or religious leader to be interested in the content of the ceremony. The lodge adviser, or his designee, may discuss the content of the ceremony and any other issues brought to his attention by one of these interested and responsible adults, with the understanding that the adult will maintain the confidentiality of the ceremony.&rdquo; It also states: &ldquo;If after discussing the ceremony with the lodge adviser, the parent, Scout leader, or religious leader continues to have questions about the content of the ceremony, that person will be permitted to read the ceremony text. Following this, parents will be in a position to decide whether to allow their son to participate in the ceremony. Candidates may not become members of the Order of the Arrow without completing the pre-Ordeal and Ordeal ceremonies.&rdquo; In the end, the scout executive has the ability to permit exceptions to this guideline. In that case, the scout executive should be made aware of the steps taken to help the parent understand the induction process and then allow or disallow the request to view the ceremony, articulating that there is to be quiet observation only, without camera, video, or voice recording. Finally, on the role of mystery in the Ordeal process, Page 47 states: &ldquo;Arrowmen maintain an air of mystery about the Order and its ceremonies because of the attractive role mystery plays. To maintain mystery, the Order restricts the pre-Ordeal and Ordeal ceremonies to candidates and members. Other ceremonies of the Order are conducted the same way.&rdquo; It is strongly encouraged, in order to keep the evening focused on the candidate, that non-members not attend any of our ceremonies. I see nothing wrong with non-members attending the post-Ordeal banquet. Sure, you may need to tailor what you say in the new member orientation, but having parents sharing in the joy and recognition of their loved one has many benefits when membership renewal time comes. You might even turn it into a public recognition of joining the organization. Don&rsquo;t forget this is also the time to plant the seed of sealing their membership with the Brotherhood. I hope this helps! Thanks for doing what you do! Best, Mike </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T21:52:54-07:00","id":1199583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1199575#post1199575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one of the sub-organizations of the Boy Scouts in the United States, the Order of the Arrow, is about cheerful service to others. I'm not going to divulge details from my time in the Scouts and as a Brotherhood Member of the Order of the Arrow, but the point of the Ordeal is to prepare oneself for service.<br /> <br /> All of the Traditions could get behind the general idea of the Order of the Arrow. The Order of Hermes would definitely find it a good place for recruits.<br /> <br /> As for how well this Hermetic Project works, remember that Scout troops differ in their effectiveness at teaching morals and thinking and teamwork. Some troops have good leaders who develop boys into good young men and other troops are badly lead.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Boy Scouts had a Fingerprinting merit badge at one point and do offer badges in a variety of fields, so a Euthanatoi could learn a lot in the Scouts.<br /> <br /> As an Outer Mystery, this isn't a bad one. The Hermetics will have to figure out who's blindly Obedient and who is Obedient and curious so they can decide which candidates to move into the inner circles and on the fast-track to Ascension.<br /> <br /> Order of the Arrow secrecy link:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://oa-scouting.org/themes/oascouting-theme/images/og/oa-social-stamp-og.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents\" target=\"_blank\"> Ask the Chairman - Ordeal Guests/Parents </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents\" target=\"_blank\"> https://oa-bsa.org/article/ask-chairman-ordeal-guestsparents </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Q: Hello Mike, I was wondering if there is any specific policy regarding having non-member guests and parents attend an Ordeal banquet. In the past, we have been allowing guests to come to our Ordeal banquet, which is held right after the Ordeal ceremony on Saturday night. This is when we also do our new member orientation. We figured that it would be best if parents could attend the orientation so they could get information about the Order of the Arrow. However, we have been receiving guests who are not parents and who are non-members. This has presented some problems as sometimes we have difficulty preventing some non-members from attending the Ordeal ceremony, and we had to tailor our orientation so it does not reveal any safeguarded material. Is there any policy or recommendation regarding whether guests are allowed at the Ordeal banquet after the Ordeal ceremony, and whether they are allowed to attend the new member orientation? Thank you for your help. In WWW, Elliott A: Elliott, The simple answer is that there is no prohibitive policy on such guests. Many lodges encourage the attendance of parents and Scout leaders at the banquet/orientation. I think it is a great strategy to get parents and other responsible parties really engaged and understanding the importance of membership in the Order. What the National OA Committee has been clear about is who should attend the actual ceremony. My suggestion is that you police that attendance carefully. I pulled out a couple statements from the 2015 printing of the Order of the Arrow Handbook that you might reference. Page 34 of the 2015 edition states: &ldquo;Youth and adult candidates for membership into the Order of the Arrow are introduced to the Order&rsquo;s concepts of servant leadership through a safeguarded ceremonial induction. Non-members should not attend the ceremonies. The Order of the Arrow recognizes and respects the right of any parent, Scout leader, or religious leader to be interested in the content of the ceremony. The lodge adviser, or his designee, may discuss the content of the ceremony and any other issues brought to his attention by one of these interested and responsible adults, with the understanding that the adult will maintain the confidentiality of the ceremony.&rdquo; It also states: &ldquo;If after discussing the ceremony with the lodge adviser, the parent, Scout leader, or religious leader continues to have questions about the content of the ceremony, that person will be permitted to read the ceremony text. Following this, parents will be in a position to decide whether to allow their son to participate in the ceremony. Candidates may not become members of the Order of the Arrow without completing the pre-Ordeal and Ordeal ceremonies.&rdquo; In the end, the scout executive has the ability to permit exceptions to this guideline. In that case, the scout executive should be made aware of the steps taken to help the parent understand the induction process and then allow or disallow the request to view the ceremony, articulating that there is to be quiet observation only, without camera, video, or voice recording. Finally, on the role of mystery in the Ordeal process, Page 47 states: &ldquo;Arrowmen maintain an air of mystery about the Order and its ceremonies because of the attractive role mystery plays. To maintain mystery, the Order restricts the pre-Ordeal and Ordeal ceremonies to candidates and members. Other ceremonies of the Order are conducted the same way.&rdquo; It is strongly encouraged, in order to keep the evening focused on the candidate, that non-members not attend any of our ceremonies. I see nothing wrong with non-members attending the post-Ordeal banquet. Sure, you may need to tailor what you say in the new member orientation, but having parents sharing in the joy and recognition of their loved one has many benefits when membership renewal time comes. You might even turn it into a public recognition of joining the organization. Don&rsquo;t forget this is also the time to plant the seed of sealing their membership with the Brotherhood. I hope this helps! Thanks for doing what you do! Best, Mike </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to blow your cover, but I think you just posted a link to a real-ass secret society run by real-ass wizards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T21:56:13-07:00","id":1199586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1199583#post1199583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to blow your cover, but I think you just posted a link to a real-ass secret society run by real-ass wizards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense. It's obviously a front organization, for <i>another</i> front organization, for a secret society. Real-ass wizards would never let themselves be so directly connected to a publicly known group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T22:14:29-07:00","id":1199592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1199586#post1199586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonsense. It's obviously a front organization, for <i>another</i> front organization, for a secret society. Real-ass wizards would never let themselves be so directly connected to a publicly known group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. Sorry, I'm still new to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T09:23:41-07:00","id":1199733,"title":"","content":"Now i am picturing a former Euthantos assassin making a room full of 12 year old Foresters quiet with his quite scary facial scars then suddenly being one of the nicest guys in the world.<br /> <br /> One idea i had for the Foresters is that if any mage wants to be a instructor they have to pass a series of tests. One of which is sucessfully doing a Forester class made out of entirely of first years, who are usually 11 or 12. Oddly enough, this knocks out most canidates. I wonder how each Trad would handle this situation without snapping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T09:57:50-07:00","id":1199746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1199733#post1199733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea i had for the Foresters is that if any mage wants to be a instructor they have to pass a series of tests. One of which is sucessfully doing a Forester class made out of entirely of first years, who are usually 11 or 12. Oddly enough, this knocks out most canidates. I wonder how each Trad would handle this situation without snapping?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's get the easy ones out of the way first:<br /> <br /> Choristers have community outreach as their bread and butter. They would have an easy time teaching kids morality, even if they don't inject theological dogma into it. They may be strict, but they shouldn't have any more trouble than any other adult more concerned with teaching kids moral lessons rather than academic ones.<br /> <br /> When you take off the edgy veneer of sex and drugs, the Ecstatic Paradigm is really just that having fun and feeling good is a good thing. I don't think it will be hard to sell children on that.<br /> <br /> Etherites shouldn't have a hard time either. Teaching kids to be creative and curious may not be easy, but it's immensely rewarding, especially to someone as passionate about Science as your average Etherite. I mean, it's not for nothing that the irl Boy Scouts have a robotics merit badge.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Verbena have an easy in road. Just teach the kids to respect nature. That's it. As long as you don't bring up the stuff about blood magick and human sacrifice, you're golden.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Now for some of the slightly more difficult ones (the Eauthanatos have already discussed extensively, so I won't mention them):<br /> <br /> Your average VA is stereotyped as surly and impatient, which doesn't mix well with children. Still, that's a generalization. I'd imagine that the Adepts would rather take in those Foresters that actively show interest in their spheres of influence, rather than going looking for them.<br /> <br /> For Dreamspeakers, Paradigm and Practice are very closely tied to culture. On one hand, I'd say most 21st century parents would jump at the chance to expose their kid to a foreign culture and become more open-minded and cosmopolitan. On the other hand, the Dreamspeaker in question should probably get used to the kids accidentally disrespecting their culture, recognizing that they're just kids and don't tend to do such things out of prejudice, but simple obliviousness.<br /> <br /> You'd think that, since it's <i>their </i>organization, the Hermetics would have it easy, but integrating all but the most basic parts of the Hermetic Paradigm into the curriculum would be a bad idea. I'd say that, like others have said, the Order would mostly use the organization as a screening process vet potential apprentices, while subtly teaching their more &quot;acceptable&quot; practices (Astrology, Mythology, etc.) to a wider demographic.<br /> <br /> The big outlier here are the Akashics. For some reason, their philosophy strikes me as the most &quot;adult&quot;, being all about self-control and moderation. I have trouble thinking of a way to make it &quot;kid-friendly&quot; without turning it into the kind of &quot;karate-themed daycare&quot; the Brotherhood hates so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-26-2018, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:31:15-07:00","id":1199755,"title":"","content":"You know, the human sacrifice thing is the reason i was considering having the organization not trust Verbena mages being alone with the Foresters. Even though they probably won't do it, the average Hermetic may think differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T08:07:03-07:00","id":1200038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197883-advice-on-a-hermetic-project?p=1198734#post1198734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because the Technocracy doesn't KNOW about every hedge wizard. Their secrecy and subtlety is key to their survival, and both Sorcerer books have explicitly stated this as being the case. Any effort to train people in Sorcery, therefore, must be done with the utmost secrecy, or they risk attracting the Union's attention. Especially if it's a Traditions effort, because the Union keeps an eye out for their sorts of magical methods. Every camp that advertises itself as being religious or devoted to martial arts, for instance, gets flagged by automated systems as being worth keeping an eye on.<br /> <br /> Hell, the fact that this is a Sorcery-training program that exists as a Public organization makes secrecy all the more important. At least with secret societies or one-on-one apprenticeships, there's a limited visibility inherent in the arrangement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering the extensive amount of abuse and psuedoscience that comes from &quot;conversion&quot; camps. I find this PROFOUNDLY unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}